An involute is a particular type of curve that is dependent on another shape or curve. 
An example of the involute of a curve is the IOCUS of a ponit on a piece of taut string as the string is either unwrapped around the curve. 


An involute curve - is a specific type of curve traced by the end of a taut string as it is unwrapped from or wrapped around another shpae or base curve. 
